course: dictionary
lesson: 9853
title: Syllables and syllabic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A syllable is a beat in a word, a part of a word you can clap. «Happy» has two claps: hap-py. Syllabic is the adjective that means about syllables.
explain: Some writing works by syllables, not single letters. «Cree syllabics were developed in the 1840s by the missionary James Evans with Cree speakers.» The word "script" tells you this is about writing, and "syllabics" tells you the symbols stand for syllables.
explain: Use the words around a new word to check your meaning. Swap in "about syllables" for "syllabic" in «Cree syllabics» and see if it still makes sense. If it does, you have understood it.
fact: A syllable is a beat in a word, and you can clap it.
fact: «Happy» has two syllables: hap-py.
fact: A syllabic writing system, called a syllabary, uses one symbol for each syllable.
fact: Japanese kana and the Cherokee syllabary are syllabic writing systems.
fact: In phonetics, a syllabic sound such as the "n" in «button» makes a syllable on its own, without a vowel.
exercise: How many syllables does «happy» have? | One | Three | Four | *Two
exercise: A syllabary uses one symbol for each what? | Word | Letter | *Syllable | Sound
exercise: How many claps does «button» need? | Four | *Two | Three | One
test: Syllabic means about what? | Colours | Letters that are silent | Numbers only | *Syllables, the beats of a word
test: In «Cree syllabics were developed in the 1840s», what kind of writing are syllabics? | A kind of music | A kind of farming | A script where each symbol stands for a whole sentence | *A script where each symbol stands for a syllable
exam: In the phrase «syllabic verse», what does syllabic describe? | *The syllables that make up each line | Speed of a runner | Length of the title | Colour of the page
